<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Sir John has been back to his usual walks of three to four miles, with hills, for more than three weeks, and the cough has gone. His home readings over the past week average 127/79 on amlodipine 5 mg, with no side effects. He has lost 3.2 kg since intake and his waist is down 4 cm. He had a symptom-limited exercise treadmill test this morning. His fecal immunochemical test and his HIV, hepatitis C and hepatitis B screening tests were negative, and he has had both rabies doses. He has been fitted for cold-weather clothing and has gone through the expedition&apos;s food lists with the purser. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Home readings</td><td>Seven-day average 127/79 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Weight</td><td>87.6 kg, from 90.8 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Exercise test</td><td>9 minutes of the Bruce protocol, about 10 METs; no ischemia</td></tr><tr><td>Screening</td><td>Fecal immunochemical test, HIV, hepatitis C and hepatitis B screening negative</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

