  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Essential hypertension on amlodipine (I10)</content>. At goal: home average 127/79 and office 128/78 on amlodipine 5 mg, helped by weight loss and less wine. Exercise test normal: about 10 METs, normal blood pressure response and no ischemia, so there is no cardiac limit on strenuous work. [S]<list><item>Continue amlodipine 5 mg; a three-year supply to be dispensed at the pre-departure visit.</item><item>Home monitor and spare cuff to travel with him; weekly readings on board, and the dose plan in writing for the ship&apos;s surgeons.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Obesity, class 1 (E66.811)</content>. 3.2 kg lost by his own plan; he wants to keep up daily exercise on board. [S]<list><item>Continue walking and portion control; deck exercise routine on board.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Expedition preparation (Z71.84)</content>. Cleared for strenuous work; cold-weather clothing fitted; food lists reviewed. [S]<list><item>Second hepatitis B dose today.</item><item>Pre-departure visit two weeks before sailing.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Office blood pressure (seated, five minutes&apos; rest, large cuff, average of two readings)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>128/78 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Home blood pressure monitoring</td><td>At diagnosis and two to four weeks after each treatment change, then weekly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Average 127/79 mmHg: at goal</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight, BMI and waist</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>87.6 kg, BMI 30.3, waist 102 cm</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Cardiac auscultation</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No murmur or gallop</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Amlodipine safety: ankle swelling, dizziness, flushing</td><td>At each visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No ankle swelling or dizziness</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Exercise treadmill test before strenuous remote work</td><td>Before clearance</td><td>Completed today</td><td>About 10 METs; peak heart rate 152; normal blood pressure response; no ischemia or arrhythmia</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Basic metabolic panel, potassium and eGFR</td><td>Yearly (every six months only on a diuretic or renin-angiotensin blocker)</td><td>Due</td><td>A baseline before departure at the next visit</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Cold injury and hypothermia prevention</td><td>Before departure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Layered clothing with vapor control fitted; buddy checks, dry socks and mitts, and frostbite and hypothermia first aid reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Nutrition and food safety for the expedition (vitamin C and D, rations, cans, lead, botulism)</td><td>Before departure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Food lists reviewed: canned food from suppliers without lead solder; damaged or bulging cans discarded unopened; vitamin C tablets in sealed storage</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Confirm or exclude hypertension with a week of home readings. Outcome by 2026-01-27: Home average 144/90 mmHg: stage 2 hypertension confirmed [S]</item><item>Blood pressure below 130/80 mmHg at home before departure. Outcome by 2026-04-07: Home average 127/79 mmHg at eight weeks on amlodipine 5 mg with lifestyle change [S]</item><item>Lose about 5 percent of body weight before sailing by his own plan of walking, hill work and smaller portions. In progress; target 2026-05-05 [S]</item><item>Medical clearance for the command with a written expedition health plan, medical kit and evacuation plan. In progress; target 2026-05-05 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Hepatitis B vaccine (HepB-CpG), second of two doses [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, hypertension and hyperlipidemia monographs (2026); Wilderness Medical Society Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Prevention and Treatment of Frostbite: 2024 Update (2024); Wilderness Medical Society Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Out-of-Hospital Evaluation and Treatment of Accidental Hypothermia: 2019 Update (2019); Clinical Guidelines for Diagnosis and Treatment of Botulism, 2021 (2021); Recommendations for medical management of adult lead exposure (2007); Weight Loss to Prevent Obesity-Related Morbidity and Mortality in Adults: Behavioral Interventions (2018)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Pre-departure visit in four weeks with a basic metabolic panel, vitamin D, PHQ-9 and GAD-7, the second zoster dose, and the medical kit and evacuation plan. Next scheduled visit 2026-05-05: pre-departure review two weeks before sailing: blood pressure, medicines and supplies, mental health, vaccinations, the medical kit and the evacuation plan. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
